 "notes": "Started p. 53 row 8 at numeral 133 (ḥa - k); stopped p. 56 row 2 at 'pu' before PLATE XI heading. p. 55 has only 8 printed rows (not 9 as the brief says); 'àpt-[f]' is in row 8, and its brackets are only in the transliteration. Overlines (rubric): p. 53 row 9 from ki to end; p. 54 row 1 from su to sauti (Àusàr not under it); p. 55 row 3 pu..su; row 5 ki, t'eṭ; row 6 àr..ṭep; row 7 ḥenen..t'eṭ (first six words) and àr; row 8 pesteχ-nek..unen; p. 56 row 1 àr only. Numerals splitting words: 134 inside sau (p. 54 r1), 135 inside qemet-nef (p. 54 r2), 139 inside qemam-k (p. 54 r8): those words keep the earlier line. The wigged seated figure (no arms visible) is coded A40 throughout (Reḥu, untu, Sami, neter, menḥu). Kneeling man with hand to face coded A2 (seḥurà, meri-k, ren, senṭ, trà). Flat oval with right tab = D46 (t'eṭ, peṭes, pest, ānṭ, ḥaṭ); flat bar with small central tie = Y1. The untransliterated group T22 Z1 O1 at end of p. 55 row 1 is entered with empty budge. No lacunae seen."
